            <ArticleTitle>Surgery of complex coronary arteriovenous fistula.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>169-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A rare type of coronary arteriovenous fistula with multiple supplying vessels from both coronary arteries and draining into the pulmonary artery was found in a 52-year-old woman with angina pectoris. The fistula was successfully closed by division of the vessels draining into the pulmonary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
